## Fault (from the orchestrator brief)

The asset read as a cream pot with a red rim band, not as a pot of paint. The paint was a mound
above the rim. The red band had the paint colour. The render camera sits near rim height, so a pool
inside the cup is not seen.

## Changes made (exact, as briefed)

1. `assets/paint-pot.ts`:
   - Removed the red body band and its `BAND`/`BAND_Y`/`smoothstep` code. The body is cream
     #efe6d2, matte, roughness 0.85. The ear stays cream.
   - Added one foot body: a brown #8a5a35 ring (`sdf.torus(0.0252, 0.003)` at y = 0.003), 0.006 m
     tall, about 1.2 mm proud of the base flare, bottom on y = 0.
   - Removed the paint mound. Added a flat paint surface at `RIM_TOP - 0.003` (0.0768 m), a
     cylinder of radius 0.0252 that fills the inner radius, roughness 0.3.
   - Added three paint runs (`paintRun`), measured from the rim top: front 0 degrees, 0.040 m;
     50 degrees toward +X, 0.028 m; 200 degrees, 0.034 m. Each run is a chain of radius 0.0026 at
     the lip up to 0.006 on the wall: a 0.0108 m wide band that stands 0.003 m proud of the
     0.0313 m wall, with a rounded 0.0044 m end. A flattened ellipsoid on the rim top makes the
     lip: 11 mm wide, 9 mm deep, 3 mm thick.
   - The surface, the lips, and the drips are one `paint` body with `color: k.tint('paint')`, so
     every preset recolours all of them. The 4 presets and their colours are unchanged.
   - Size kept: 0.072 x 0.084 x 0.069 m, bottom on y = 0, centred, facing +Z, 2,218 triangles in
     the final build (3,263 before reduction).
2. `measure/tracks/asset_chibi_sprouts_r1_20261022/plan.md`: one sub-bullet under the props task.
